{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01TKJritvLW26Zv78h6HjSCi", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.singulart.com/blog/en/?p=134145\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nationalacademy.emuseum.com/people/4433/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.annexgalleries.com/artists/biography/2151\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:24:59.521Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Richard Serra first outdoor sculptures country", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01V1YYuLrhfRyoBcwcc2c4d8", "content": [{"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "untappedcities.com", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965"}, {"title": "richard serras first major outdoor installation was located at 183rd street in the bronx nyc", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc"}, {"title": "Artists in the History", "url": "https://www.singulart.com/blog/en/?p=134145"}, {"title": "Richard Serra, sculptor of massive masterworks", "url": "https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294"}, {"title": "richard serra audio biography  6134072", "url": "https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra"}, {"title": "American, 1938 - 2024", "url": "https://nationalacademy.emuseum.com/people/4433/richard-serra"}, {"title": "Richard Serra Biography", "url": "https://www.annexgalleries.com/artists/biography/2151"}]}, "The sources disagree on which work came first, so I'd treat the answer as contested.\n\n- **Pulitzer Piece (St. Louis, Missouri):** The Guggenheim Bilbao timeline says Serra created his first site-specific work and the first of his large outdoor sculptures with this piece near Saint Louis. The same timeline has him showing an outdoor work using curved steel at the LACMA exhibition Art and Technology in 1971 (Semi-Circular Elevational Steps).\n- **To Encircle Base Plate Hexagon (Bronx, New York):** Untapped Cities calls this his first major outdoor exhibition. It says that in 1970 he approached the New York City Park Administration about creating his first installation somewhere in the city, and the site was at 183rd Street and Webster Avenue.\n- **Conflicting claim:** One podcast-style source says Serra made his first large-scale outdoor sculpture in 1968 and installed it on a Long Island beach. This conflicts with the 1970 Bronx date from Untapped Cities, and the source looks unreliable, so I'd discount it.\n- **Later outdoor work:** Shift, a set of concrete walls, was created in 1970–72 in King City, Ontario, Canada, according to the same podcast source (item 7-11).\n\nOverall, the most consistent reading is that his first major outdoor works date to about 1970–71, in the United States, with the Bronx and St. Louis pieces both cited as early candidates. Checking a museum catalogue or a scholarly Serra monograph would settle which he himself counts as first."], "durationSeconds": 7.711048125000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01TKJritvLW26Zv78h6HjSCi", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
