{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Dtu8BYaaEzbZYB7sm4Yq9x", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shift_(sculpture)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://WWW.ATLASOBSCURA.COM/places/shift-richard-serra-king-city-ontario\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hyperallergic.com/early-richard-serra-land-work-finally-gets-cultural-protection\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hyperallergic.com/in-search-of-richard-serras-embattled-shift\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.eraarch.ca/?p=8308\"}, {\"url\": \"https://media.blogto.com/arts/2009/12/searching_for_richard_serras_shift_in_king_city\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hyperallergic.com/early-richard-serra-land-work-finally-gets-cultural-protection.md\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.blogto.com/arts/2012/08/richard_serras_shift_under_threat_once_again/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://spacing.ca/toronto/2009/12/10/richard-serras-king-city-shift/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://skyrisecities.com/forum/goto/post?id=134424\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:25:08.968Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Richard Serra Shift King City Ontario first outdoor sculpture Canada", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01BkDJHZmCHkjCGQDgaf6aBR", "content": [{"title": "Shift (sculpture)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shift_(sculpture)"}, {"title": "shift richard serra king city ontario", "url": "https://WWW.ATLASOBSCURA.COM/places/shift-richard-serra-king-city-ontario"}, {"title": "Early Richard Serra Land Work Finally Gets Cultural Protection", "url": "https://hyperallergic.com/early-richard-serra-land-work-finally-gets-cultural-protection"}, {"title": "In Search of Richard Serra's Embattled \"Shift\"", "url": "https://hyperallergic.com/in-search-of-richard-serras-embattled-shift"}, {"title": "www.eraarch.ca", "url": "https://www.eraarch.ca/?p=8308"}, {"title": "Richard Serra Shift", "url": "https://media.blogto.com/arts/2009/12/searching_for_richard_serras_shift_in_king_city"}, {"title": "> ## Content Index", "url": "https://hyperallergic.com/early-richard-serra-land-work-finally-gets-cultural-protection.md"}, {"title": "Richard Serra Shift", "url": "https://www.blogto.com/arts/2012/08/richard_serras_shift_under_threat_once_again/"}, {"title": "richard serras king city shift", "url": "https://spacing.ca/toronto/2009/12/10/richard-serras-king-city-shift/"}, {"title": "skyrisecities.com", "url": "https://skyrisecities.com/forum/goto/post?id=134424"}]}, "The search supports that Shift is an early Serra work in King City, but it doesn't establish that it was his first outdoor sculpture.\n\n- **Basics:** Wikipedia describes Shift as a large outdoor sculpture by Serra, commissioned in 1970 by art collector Roger Davidson and installed on his family property. It consists of six large concrete forms, each 20 centimetres thick and 1.5 metres high.\n- **Early career:** Sources call it an early work rather than the first. One says Shift is one of Serra's earliest site-specific installations. Another calls it an important early piece of land art and a relatively early work in the career of Richard Serra.\n- **Materials:** One source notes that the completed sculpture, entitled Shift, is one of only two works that Serra ever created in concrete.\n- **Heritage status:** Sources report that King City council moved to protect the work. One says the township council for King City, Ontario, voted last week to officially designate the sculpture a site of \"cultural heritage value.\" The date of that vote isn't clear from the results; the sources mention votes in 2008, 2012 and 2013.\n- **Location:** Distance from Toronto varies by source. Wikipedia says about 30 km, Hyperallergic says 50 km, and BlogTO says about 40 km."], "durationSeconds": 5.631297125000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Dtu8BYaaEzbZYB7sm4Yq9x", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
