{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_017xcgD2VTRNsCz99X6eRfwi", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965\"}, {\"url\": \"https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.pressreader.com/new-zealand/the-post-1022/20240330/282097756713076\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nationalacademy.emuseum.com/people/4433/richard-serra\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:25:17.210Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Richard Serra\" \"first outdoor sculptures\" ", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_012nfg6bciYd9wuTkntrLmNQ", "content": [{"title": "untappedcities.com", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/?p=465965"}, {"title": "richard serras first major outdoor installation was located at 183rd street in the bronx nyc", "url": "https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc"}, {"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://pro.guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "Serra, Richard", "url": "https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra"}, {"title": "richard serra audio biography  6134072", "url": "https://www.spreaker.com/podcast/richard-serra-audio-biography--6134072"}, {"title": "Creator of monumental works that transformed public spaces", "url": "https://www.pressreader.com/new-zealand/the-post-1022/20240330/282097756713076"}, {"title": "Richard Serra", "url": "https://www.Britannica.com/summary/Richard-Serra"}, {"title": "Richard Serra, sculptor of massive masterworks", "url": "https://www.pressreader.com/usa/the-day/20240404/281784224111294"}, {"title": "American, 1938 - 2024", "url": "https://nationalacademy.emuseum.com/people/4433/richard-serra"}]}, "The search turned up conflicting answers to what Serra's first outdoor sculpture was.\n\n- **Bronx installation (1970):** Untapped Cities identifies his first major outdoor work as To Encircle Base Plate Hexagon, Right Angles Inverted, at 183rd Street and Webster Avenue in the Bronx. It says the Park Administration offered a permit to work on a street in the Bronx for $250.\n- **St. Louis (Pulitzer Piece):** The Guggenheim Bilbao collection timeline calls Pulitzer Piece: Stepped Elevation near Saint Louis, Missouri the first of his large outdoor sculptures and his first site-specific work. It does not give a year in the excerpt.\n- **Long Island beach (1968):** An audio biography on Spreaker says that in 1968 Serra made a large outdoor piece with the same title as the Bronx work, installed on a Long Island beach. This conflicts with the Bronx account and with the other sources, so I would treat it as unreliable.\n\nThe most likely answer is that the Bronx piece was his first major outdoor work, while the Guggenheim timeline points to the St. Louis piece as the first of his large outdoor sculptures. Those two sources don't contradict each other directly, since they use different criteria (\"major outdoor exhibition\" versus \"first large outdoor sculpture\"). Checking a dated museum or catalogue source would settle it."], "durationSeconds": 6.159852333000003, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_017xcgD2VTRNsCz99X6eRfwi", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDV5r4XnwGghQe3MZb73", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：美国（不完全确定）。**\n\n搜到的资料里，早期户外作品都在美国：\n\n- 布朗克斯（纽约）的《To Encircle Base Plate Hexagon, Right Angles Inverted》，1970 年，被称为他的第一件大型户外作品。\n- 圣路易斯附近的《Pulitzer Piece》，古根海姆毕尔巴鄂的年表称它是他最早的大型户外雕塑，也是他第一件场域特定作品。\n\n两种说法的标准不同（\"主要户外展出\"和\"大型户外雕塑\"），所以没有哪一个被直接确认为\"第一件\"。\n\n加拿大安大略省的《Shift》（1970–72）只被称为早期作品，没有资料说它是第一件。有一个播客来源说 1968 年他在长岛海滩做过户外作品，但它与其他来源矛盾，我没有采信。\n\n我没有找到一份注明年份的美术馆或专著来源来定论。\n\nSources:\n- [Untapped Cities：布朗克斯的第一件大型户外作品](https://untappedcities.com/richard-serras-first-major-outdoor-installation-was-located-at-183rd-street-in-the-bronx-nyc)\n- [Guggenheim Bilbao：Serra 年表](https://guggenheim-bilbao.eus/en/the-collection/artists/richard-serra)\n- [Wikipedia：Shift (sculpture)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shift_(sculpture))"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1230, "cache_read_input_tokens": 6912, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1230}, "output_tokens": 519, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:25:22.107Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDV5qkusQsEy26VvTxve"}
